  "status": "experimental",
  "hypothesis": "Phase 2: the adopted class-skill kit creates the counter-cycle without any edge deciding the matchup screen, on the keel baseline (#169), measured by the eight-entrant wave-4 population (three strikers, three bulwarks, two fabricators; two lineages are skill-native and fresh). Pre-registered per-cell predictions: bulwark-vs-striker moves >= +0.30 toward the bulwark with kit on and reaches >= -0.10 (the refuted cycle leg; the shell is the instrument); striker-vs-fabricator keeps its sign and softens (|delta| <= 0.25); bulwark-vs-fabricator carries NO sign prediction (seed-noise per #157) with a balance target |payoff| < 0.35. Edge band: every cross-class edge with kit on lands at |payoff| in [0.15, 0.40] - below is no cycle, above is the matchup screen deciding the game. Do-no-harm keel gates: cap share and draw rate on kit-on cells must not exceed the kit-off anchors by more than 0.05, and leader-extends must not fall below 0.45 of its anchor value. Validity gate with a measured-decline clause: a skill under 25% usage where legal is an adoption question UNLESS an author's DX records a priced decline (the wave-4 striker mirrors measured declining-to-cast as winning play; a decline is doctrine, not non-adoption). Disclosures: striker-mirror cells carry identical rules bytes for striker-only vs universal bend (keel==veer, helm==rig by rules fingerprint) and must not be read as independent bend evidence; the placement tag rations stance availability (~6% of standoff striker ticks) and the break budget never fired in wave-4 self-play - phase 2 measures the kit AS IS, and the tuning pass owns those knobs; leave-one-skill-out restricted-play arms are deferred to the tuning pass with their own spec; no viewing pass gates this factorial - the owner watchability gallery follows the holdout as the phase-2 human gate.",
